Muesli includes software vendored from FluidAudio
(https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

The vendored sources live in:
  native/MuesliNative/Sources/MuesliCore/Qwen3ASR/

A copy of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is included alongside those
sources in LICENSE-Apache-2.0. The files were copied from FluidAudio
v0.15.1 (ASR/Qwen3/) and renamed with a MuesliQwen3 prefix; this
distribution preserves that origin and license.

Muesli includes AI Elements Swift (native/AIElementsSwift), an independent
SwiftUI adaptation of Vercel AI Elements concepts, licensed under Apache-2.0.
It includes Lucide icons under ISC/MIT. Attribution, pinned revisions, and
complete license notices are retained in native/AIElementsSwift/NOTICE and
native/AIElementsSwift/Licenses/.

Muesli's MLX speech-recognition model ports (the Qwen3-ASR and Granite Speech
backends built on the MLX ASR layer in docs/mlx-asr-backends.md) are ports of
model code from mlx-audio-swift (https://github.com/Blaizzy/mlx-audio-swift),
licensed under the MIT License. No mlx-audio-swift file is copied by the shared
layer itself; each port file that is derived from it names its source file and
the pinned commit in its header. Upstream license text:

